# LancarSec .gitignore
#
# Deny by intent. This repository ships source, bundled data, and docs.
# It does not ship anything generated, anything secret, or anything an
# operator supplies at runtime.
#
# Two things are deliberately NOT ignored and must stay tracked:
#   examples/config.json        - the template operators copy to config.json
#   global/fingerprints/*.json  - bundled TLS fingerprint data read at startup
# Defensive re-includes for both are at the bottom of this file.

# --- Operator config: never commit a live one -----------------------------
# Root-anchored on purpose so examples/config.json is untouched.
/config.json
/config.*.json
/config.json.bak
**/config.json
**/config.*.json
*.local.json
**/.env
**/.env.*
*.env
secrets.json
**/secrets.json
kubeconfig
*.kubeconfig
backup.sql
dump.sql
*.sql

# --- Private keys, certificates, key material -----------------------------
# assets/server/server.key was a genuine RSA key (CN=baloo.dog, ZeroSSL,
# expired 2023-03-17) that shipped to every clone. It is untracked and deleted
# as of this commit; the history purge is a separate, later step. Treat the key
# as permanently burned - never issue a new cert against it. Nothing that looks
# like key material is allowed back into this tree.
*.key
*.pem
*.crt
*.cer
*.der
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
*.gpg
*.asc
id_rsa
id_ed25519
id_ecdsa
id_dsa
*.ppk
.ssh/
.htpasswd
.netrc

# --- Databases and runtime state ------------------------------------------
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*Cache.db*

# --- Runtime output -------------------------------------------------------
crash.log
*.log

# --- Build output ---------------------------------------------------------
# 'main' is what the Dockerfile (go build -o main .) and the release workflow
# (go build -o dist/main) produce; 88 revisions of it sit in history awaiting
# the purge. 'oryxBuildBinary' was a tracked Azure Oryx artifact, untracked as
# of this commit.
/main
/lancarsec
/lancarsec_*
/oryxBuildBinary
/dist/
/bin/
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# --- Go test, coverage, profiling -----------------------------------------
*.test
*.out
coverage.out
coverage.txt
coverage.html
*.cover
*.prof
*.pprof
__debug_bin*
go.work
go.work.sum
# Uncomment only if this project ever vendors its dependencies.
# vendor/

# --- Agent and tooling scratch -------------------------------------------
# Claude Code puts subagent git worktrees under .claude/worktrees/. They are
# real checkouts of this repo and must never be committed into it.
.claude/

# --- Editors and OS noise -------------------------------------------------
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/tasks.json
!.vscode/launch.json
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/*.code-snippets
.history/
.history
.ionide
*.vsix
.idea/
*.iml
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Must stay tracked ----------------------------------------------------
# No rule above matches these; the re-includes are here so a future edit that
# adds a broad *.json or config* rule cannot silently untrack them. This only
# works against file-pattern rules: git cannot re-include a file that sits
# under an excluded DIRECTORY, so never add a rule like 'global/' or 'examples/'.
!examples/config.json
# The load harness ships a config with placeholder secrets and a 127.0.0.1
# backend. It matches **/config.*.json above, which is the rule that stops an
# operator committing a live one, so it needs an explicit exception.
!hack/config.test.json
!global/fingerprints/*.json
!global/proxy/version.json
